{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a reusable asynchronous operation and choose the policies that surround it."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Getting started","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"TaskLoom"}],"role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CancellationAndRetries","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/TaskLifetimes","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CombineAndDispatch"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Installation","anchor":"Installation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/github.com\/modern-swift-dev\/taskloom-swift.git"},{"type":"text","text":" using Swift Package Manager, select the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main"},{"type":"text","text":" branch during the prerelease period, and add the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TaskLoom"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your target. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import TaskLoom"},{"type":"text","text":" in source files. Pin a revision if you need a reproducible dependency before the first release."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Compose an operation","anchor":"Compose-an-operation"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import TaskLoom","","let operation = AsyncOperation {","    try Task.checkCancellation()","    return 42","}",".retry(3, backoff: .constant(.milliseconds(100)))",".timeout(.seconds(2))","","let result = try await operation.execute()"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncOperation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" accepts a sendable asynchronous closure and returns a sendable result. Every execution runs the closure again. Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncTask","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for work that returns a value without throwing. Its timeout takes a default value because failure is not part of its result type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"text":" to transform a result and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMap"},{"text":" to select subsequent work. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"all"},{"text":" runs operations concurrently and preserves their input order in the resulting array. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"allSettled"},{"text":" omits failed operations; it does not return failure records.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Limit concurrent work","anchor":"Limit-concurrent-work"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Share an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncSemaphore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" between operations and apply "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"limited(by:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to each one. This bounds simultaneous work; it is not a requests-per-second rate limiter. Choose a positive permit count and keep the protected work asynchronous so waiting does not block a thread. Waiting for a permit is currently not cancellation-aware: cancelling a waiting task does not remove it from the semaphore’s wait queue."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CancellationAndRetries","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" before composing timeout, retry, race, and fallback policies."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentatio